## 2.1 Identification of Independent Architectural Sub-Modules
We isolate four structural layers within the core DRVA stack to test their individual impact:

   1. V-Parser: The specialized visual vision-language sub-agent responsible for coordinate extraction.
   2. T-Auditor: The textual database cross-validator that tracks the ground-truth back-end tabular data frames.
   3. HAP Grammar: The Hierarchical Abstraction Prompt layout format applied to visual navigation instructions.
   4. Confidence Router: The probabilistic mathematical filter that stalls execution when token divergence crosses threshold bounds.

